doc episodes 5 Episode 1: "The Twelfth Man" — The supporters take centre stage.
Cold open: The episode opens on a quiet morning at the training ground.
Matchday: A family from the season-ticket waiting list gets the call they have waited eleven years for. The cameras follow them from the pub to their seats.
Training ground: A rare clean bill of health for the squad. 
Closing: The season has barely started. Next up: Arsenal Legends (Pre-season friendly) on 8 Aug. The narrator closes the episode: "In this building, there is no such thing as a quiet week." 
QUOTES Lucas Okoro (Head groundsman (series)): You hear the roar from the tunnel and the hair on your arms stands up. Thirty years and it never gets old.
T (Manager): Those people pay their money and give us everything. The least we can do is leave everything out there.
Tom Bakari (Academy player): Training with the first team this week was mad. I just tried not to give the ball away.
Narrator (Series voice-over): Results decide everything here. Even the mood in the canteen.
